---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Who we are and how we review coffee equipment. Data-driven, independent, affiliate-funded."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'About', url: '/about/' },
  ]}
>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      We help readers choose better coffee equipment by comparing real
      specifications, prices, and use cases across hundreds of products.
      Less hype, more numbers.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site is</h2>
    <p>
      An independent reviews and comparison site for coffee equipment —
      espresso machines, grinders, brewers, and accessories. Every
      product page is built from verifiable specifications, not
      generic opinions. The question we try to answer is straightforward:
      <em>which machine fits your specific use case at your specific
      budget?</em>
    </p>

    <h2>How we make money</h2>
    <p>
      We earn affiliate commission when readers buy through our product
      links. As an Amazon Associate, we earn from qualifying purchases.
      Affiliate revenue funds the site and keeps it free of paid
      advertising. We do not accept payment from manufacturers in
      exchange for coverage, and we do not accept free samples in
      exchange for rankings.
    </p>

    <h2>Editorial approach</h2>
    <p>
      Our recommendations are anchored in three things:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Verifiable specifications.</strong> Boiler type, group
        head size, burr material, PID presence, footprint, weight,
        warranty — publicly documented attributes that can be compared
        side by side.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Use-case fit.</strong> The "best" machine depends on
        whether you make milk drinks, work in a small kitchen, want
        manual control, or value low-maintenance automation. Content
        is organized around those real decisions.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Price tier transparency.</strong> Products are bucketed
        by price (budget, mid, premium, pro). Comparisons happen within
        tiers; we don't pretend a $200 machine competes with a $1500
        one — though we will tell you when the difference doesn't matter
        for your use case.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we don't do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We don't post fake reviews.</li>
      <li>We don't accept payment in exchange for ranking position.</li>
      <li>We don't recommend products outside the budget you indicated.</li>
      <li>We don't simulate first-hand testing for products we haven't actually used; comparative analysis is clearly labeled as such.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Coffee origins, briefly</h2>
    <p>
      The operator grew up in Colombia, one of the world's top
      coffee-producing countries, before relocating internationally. This
      site focuses on equipment rather than beans, but that background
      informs how we think about the machine-to-cup relationship: the
      right equipment is the one that lets a good bean show its
      character.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Reach us at <a href="mailto:hello@example.com">hello@example.com</a>.
      <em>(A permanent contact address will be published here once the
      site is on its final domain.)</em>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 2rem auto 4rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .legal-page h1 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .legal-page .lead {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: #444;
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .legal-page h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .legal-page ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }
  .legal-page li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
